<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26473" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίειμι</span></b> , serving as fut. to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διέρχομαι,</span>
		impf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διῄειν</span>: fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διείσομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					494
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				837
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>:—<i>go to and fro, roam about,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				845
			</span></i>; of a report, <i>spread,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγος διῄει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Ant.</u>
					56
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>pass through.</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ αὐτῶν μέσων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					3.21
				</span></i>
			; <i>get through, escape,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διὰ τῶν πόρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Cael.</u>
					307b13
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔξω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>CP</u>
					5.9.12
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				204a4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>pass,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμέρα χειμέριος δίεισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Sign.</u>
					46
				</span></i>
			; <i>proceed,</i> of a play, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				920
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> c. acc.,
				<i>go through, traverse,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Av.</u>
				1392
			</span></i>: c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τὸν θεῖον δρόμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ax.</u>
					370e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>go through a subject</i> in speaking or writing, <i>narrate,
				describe, discuss,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Cri.</u>
				47c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δ. τῷ λόγῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Grg.</u>
					505e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> cc., <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Icar.</u>
				3
			</span></i>.</div>
